Description: Fix a stack buffer overflow, an uninitialised sample and window close
 The _T() macro filled the sine/cosine tables from index 1 to 10000, writing
 one float past the end of each 10000-element array on the stack and leaving
 index 0 uninitialised (found with AddressSanitizer). Fill indexes 0 to 9999.
 .
 In the audio callback, the sample value v was read uninitialised when a
 buffer starts on a rest in the score; start it at 0.
 .
 The main loop only stopped on SDL_KEYDOWN, so closing the window did
 nothing; stop on SDL_QUIT too.
